en by lightest bodyweight."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/56942"} "Arkady Vorobyov"] " had won the gold medal in this class in 1956-60, but had now retired and was coaching the Soviet team. Britain’s " [:a {:href ""} "Louis Martin"] ", the 1960 bronze medalist, had won the 1962-63 World Championships and held the world record and was favored, with Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/56531"} "Ireneusz Paliński"] ", 1961 World Champion and runner-up to Martin in 1962-63, considered his biggest challenger. Nobody expected much from Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/56894"} "Vladimir Golovanov"] ", who had little international reputation, and had never even won a national title. However, Golovanov lifted 165.0 kg in the press to lead, and also had the best snatch with 142.5 kg, equalled by Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/55971"} "Árpád Nemessányi"] ". When Golovanov jerked 180.0 kg, he set a world record total of 487.5 kg to win gold in a big upset. Martin was never really close, but also lifted 180.0 kg in the clean &amp; jerk to take silver, with Paliński getting bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/56894"} "Vladimir Golovanov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "487.5"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record (equalled)"} "=WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55747"} "Louis Martin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}]